<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit 8 Lesson 6 survey project">
<h2>Survey the Class, Survey the School</h2>
<p><a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-8/lesson-6/lesson.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original 2021 survey graph and blank-table source</a>. The publisher source table pixels were not reproduced or verified.</p>
<p>In groups of four, develop one clear category-based question with <strong>at most six</strong> answer choices. Revise the categories with the teacher.</p>
<p>Choose who asks, who tallies, and how each student will be counted <strong>exactly once</strong>. Record authentic responses from a larger group, possibly over several days, and preserve the original categories and totals for the NEXT lesson graphs.</p>
<p>Teacher checks question design, real collection methods, duplicates and recorded counts. Independent numerical samples do not substitute for school survey results. Publisher restricted Cool-down excluded.</p>
</section>
